{"book":26,"chapter":44,"context":{"chapter":44,"title":"The Shut Gate and Priests","summary":"The east gate is shut because the Lord has entered by it; foreigners are barred; Levites who led Israel into idolatry are demoted; and the faithful sons of Zadok serve as priests under strict rules.","background":"Zadok was the priest who stayed loyal to David and Solomon, and his family led the Jerusalem priesthood. Ezekiel, himself a priest, holds the priests to high standards: linen, not wool (vv. 17–18), no wine on duty, careful marriages, and teaching the difference between holy and common (v. 23). God, not land, is their inheritance.","customs":[{"term":"Linen garments","verses":"44:17-18","note":"Linen was cool and clean; wool caused sweat. Priests wore only linen in the inner court and left it there."},{"term":"The prince","verses":"44:3","note":"Ezekiel's future leader is called 'prince' rather than 'king.' He has honor at the gate but serves within limits set by God."}],"watchFor":["'I am their inheritance' (v. 28)."],"connections":["Numbers 18:20","1 Kings 2:35","Leviticus 10:9-10","Malachi 2:7"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיָּשֶׁב","vaiyashev","H7725","Hc/Vhw3ms","and he brought back"],["אֹתִי","'oti","H853","HTo/Sp1bs","<obj.> me"],["דֶּרֶךְ","derekh","H1870","HNcbsc","[the] way of"],["שַׁעַר","sha'ar","H8179","HNcmsc","[the] gate of"],["הַמִּקְדָּשׁ","hamikdash","H4720","HTd/Ncmsa","the sanctuary"],["הַחִיצוֹן","hachitzon","H2435","HTd/Aamsa","<the> outer"],["הַפֹּנֶה","haponeh","H6437","HTd/Vqrmsa","which faces"],["קָדִים","kadim","H6921","HNcmsa","east"],["וְהוּא","vehu'","H1931","HC/Pp3ms","and it"],["סָגוּר","sagur","H5462","HVqsmsa","[was] shut"]],"x":[[26043001,26043001,4],[26040006,26040006,3],[26040017,26040017,3],[26042014,26042014,3]],"xn":4},"2":{"w":[["וַיֹּאמֶר","vaiyomer","H559","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he said"],["אֵלַי","'elai","H413","HR/Sp1bs","to me"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["הַשַּׁעַר","hasha'ar","H8179","HTd/Ncmsa","the gate"],[